    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0449" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.51/134a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Deputy Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>)<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d502-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-13T17:00:00-04:00">June 13, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. The French Government has been informed that when Ambassador Bullitt finds it
                    impossible to communicate with the French Government you are to act temporarily
                    as representative of the United <pb facs="0450" n="441" xml:id="pg441"/> States
                    near the French Government for the purpose of maintaining communication with
                    that Government. Therefore, when you are informed by the French Government that
                    they are no longer in communication with Ambassador Bullitt you should assume
                    this temporary function. Report immediately when you assume these duties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d502-f1" n="82" type="source" xml:id="d502-f1-content">
                <p>At this time in Angers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
